{
  "title": "110: al-Nasr النصر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا جَآءَ نَصْرُ اللّٰهِ وَالْفَتْحُۙ‏(1)\nEZAA JAAA-A NASRUL LAAHE WAL-FATHO.\nWhen cometh the help of God and the Victory\nوَرَاَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ فِىْ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ اَفْوَاجًا ۙ‏(2)\nWA RA-AYATAN NAASA YADKHOLOONA FEE DEENIL LAAHE AFWAAJAN.\nAnd thou seest people entering the religion of God in multitudes\nفَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ ؔؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ تَوَّابًا‏(3)\nFASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA WAS TAGHFIRH, INNAHU KAANA TAWWAABAA.\nCelebrate then the praise of thy Lord and seek thou His protection, (for) verily He is Oft-Turning (merciful)!",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Madinah and it has 3 verses. It is narrated that whoever recites this Surah in compulsory prayers will always be victorious over his enemies. On the Day of Judgement he will be given a book in which it will be written that he is free from hellfire.\nRecitation of this Surah in the prayers ensures that the prayers are accepted. The one who recites this Surah frequently is held in the same status as those who were with the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) when Makkah was conquered."
